Z||000000||fierospeeder||10-21-1999||06:44 PM||||I have an 84 fiero 2.5 and i was wondering is it possible to put a 2.8L in the car?  Because i dont think they made any 2.8s in 84 for that body.  If i do the 3.1 upgrade &lt;drool&gt; is it better to buy one of those pisca stroker kits or do what Hartz did and buy the parts from Summit.  <BR>Thanks you guys and the hot fiero women.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eric Marsh||10-22-1999||02:55 PM||||I can't say for sure, but I'd guess that the 84 is close enough to the 85-87 that anything from one of them would fit in your '84. Before spending lots of money you might want to consider getting a newer model that already has the features you are looking for tho...||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||10-22-1999||04:25 PM||||I can help with this.  1984 was the first year and Pontiac changed several things in 1985 on up.  If you do want to swap to the larger motor.  Get a donor car and get as much of the wiring as you can out of it.  I mean from the engine, to the ecm, all the way to the dash and front firewall.  If you do this, you wont have much of a problem, except the rear lights will require some minor modification because the main connector where all the wires connect to the engine got moved  to the battery area.  <P>I recently finished swapping an 84 4 cyl to an 85 4cyl with a 5 speed and the wiring just about killed me.  The ECM wasnt getting power , none of the gauges worked, I ended up removing the entire 85 wiring system and swapping them out with the exception of the interior, front, and rear light harnesses. <P>It took longer to straighten out the wiring then it did to remove, tune up and clean, and replace the motor.  Looking back, after all of that trouble, I should have just swapped it up to a 6 cyl.  (but I didnt have one)<P>Anyway, just my $0.02||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||10-22-1999||08:16 PM||||When I put my 86 V6 in my 88 Coupe I asked tons of questions before I started. Ed Parks told me that even though the 88 cradle is completely different it is easier than putting a V6 in an 84 Fiero. <P>BTW, I had the complete, running donor car. Looking back...if I didn't have the donr car I would never attempt it. I took something from the donor and put it in the project car so I didn't forget where it went and how it went.||||reg||3
Z||000004||superXmotorsports||10-25-1999||09:53 PM||||Fierospeeder I have a running 2.8 / 4spd here in PA if you're anywhere close.  It's in a stripped down 86 SE but all the running gear is still in place. $350 if you would be interested.||||reg||4
